WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.000
OpenTelemetry.

2
00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:07.767
The vendor-neutral standard for seeing what your system is doing, even across many services.

3
00:00:08.967 --> 00:00:13.700
OpenTelemetry, or OTel, standardizes three observability signals.

4
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:16.600
Traces follow one request through your system.

5
00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:18.667
Metrics are numbers over time.

6
00:00:18.967 --> 00:00:21.035
And logs are timestamped events.

7
00:00:21.035 --> 00:00:25.300
There are SDKs for every language and exporters for every backend.

8
00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:28.733
The core trick is context propagation.

9
00:00:29.033 --> 00:00:30.600
Service A starts a trace.

10
00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:35.800
When A calls B, the trace ID travels in an HTTP header called traceparent.

11
00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:41.067
B's spans attach to A's trace, so you get a single waterfall for the whole request.

12
00:00:42.267 --> 00:00:43.633
That's the real promise.

13
00:00:43.933 --> 00:00:50.567
For AI systems, the GenAI conventions even standardize names for model calls and token counts.

14
00:00:50.867 --> 00:00:53.267
Instrument once, and choose vendors later.

15
00:00:54.467 --> 00:00:56.033
Here's the setup in Python.

16
00:00:56.333 --> 00:01:01.167
One line instruments the FastAPI server, so every request gets a span.

17
00:01:01.467 --> 00:01:07.367
One line instruments the HTTP client, so every outgoing call carries the trace header.

18
00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:11.867
Then we add our own span around the rerank step, tagged with the model name.

19
00:01:13.067 --> 00:01:14.841
Now a real debugging story.

20
00:01:14.841 --> 00:01:17.733
Users say the agent sometimes takes forever.

21
00:01:18.033 --> 00:01:21.141
Three services, three log files, no shared ID.

22
00:01:21.141 --> 00:01:23.100
So you add OTel to all three.

23
00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:29.200
The next slow request is one trace: agent four point nine seconds, RAG four point six.

24
00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:34.889
And inside it, a three point eight second gap before the vLLM span even starts.

25
00:01:34.889 --> 00:01:39.800
That's connection pool exhaustion, obvious only in the joined waterfall.

26
00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:41.879
Let's recap.

27
00:01:41.879 --> 00:01:45.100
OTel standardizes traces, metrics, and logs.

28
00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:48.567
The traceparent header joins services into one trace.

29
00:01:48.867 --> 00:01:53.200
GenAI conventions give LLM calls shared attribute names.

30
00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:56.383
Instrument once and swap backends freely.

31
00:01:56.383 --> 00:01:58.000
Next up: Arize Phoenix.
